{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 10, :comments ["<b>A priest's resident hireling.</b> One might say: a resident — yes, but not a hireling. And I say: if a resident, whose acquisition is a permanent acquisition, does not eat, then a hireling, whose acquisition is for a term — no need to say he does not eat. Rather, were I to say this 'resident' is acquired for a term, but one acquired permanently would eat — 'hireling' comes and teaches about 'resident,' that even though he is acquired permanently, he does not eat."], :book :leviticus, :voice :chizkuni, :lang :en, :chapter 22, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T15:14:15.565207063Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}